{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rsasaki0109/rustwright/pulls/1","id":4801829552,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUhboA88AAAABHjYasA","html_url":"https://github.com/rsasaki0109/rustwright/pull/1","diff_url":"https://github.com/rsasaki0109/rustwright/pull/1.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/rsasaki0109/rustwright/pull/1.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rsasaki0109/rustwright/issues/1","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rsasaki0109/rustwright/pulls/1/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rsasaki0109/rustwright/pulls/1/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rsasaki0109/rustwright/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rsasaki0109/rustwright/issues/1/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rsasaki0109/rustwright/statuses/39e1c8951dd2ebd67cd1ef8e7311f582d418d873","number":1,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Own browser lifecycle cleanup and expand reliability verification","user":{"login":"rsasaki0109","id":18298605,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4Mjk4NjA1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18298605?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsasaki0109","html_url":"https://github.com/rsasaki0109","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsasaki0109/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsasaki0109/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsasaki0109/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsasaki0109/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsasaki0109/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsasaki0109/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsasaki0109/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsasaki0109/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsasaki0109/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Browser startup cancellation, timeout or early exit could leave a child process or temporary profile behind, and retained Firefox page handles could keep network-idle and diagnostic workers alive after closure. Startup ownership now kills and reaps the direct child before removing its owned profile, retains readable failure logs, and transfers ownership on readiness. Shared Firefox close signals and socket shutdown finish the observers even without another remote destroy event.\n\nChrome target discovery could fail when a snapshotted tab disappeared during Page.enable. After a typed detached-session initialization error, browser-level Target.getTargetInfo verifies disappearance; only its exact no-target error permits skipping that tab. Live-target initialization errors and unexpected probe errors still propagate.\n\nThe branch also hardens transport, creation and interception ownership, adds shared reload/history operations, implements acknowledged Firefox HTTP(S) network-idle observation, and corrects native browser installation/sandbox setup in required CI. A new seventh job requires complete current-version headed and alternate-version headless suites plus read-only public-site observations. Required failures remain fatal without retries.\n\nValidation already completed at source `4cdec571a26c64e123a4dde66d4d9b47e8c64f63`:\n\n- [Run 37983300059](https://github.com/rsasaki0109/rustwright/actions/runs/37983300059): all six jobs succeeded. Actual checkout merge `58ac49f` has identical blobs and modes for all 152 relevant inputs.\n- Ubuntu workspace: 475 passed, zero failed/filtered, one existing intentionally ignored macro doctest. This includes 211 library cases (111 BiDi), four compat_report example cases and 193 HTTP cases.\n- Chrome 155.0.8059.39 / Firefox 157.0.1: 79 required portable cases per Ubuntu, Windows and macOS arm64; Ubuntu also passes 114 additional HTTP cases. These repeat workspace coverage and are not summed as unique tests.\n- Rust 1.85 locked all-target compilation, stable Clippy and formatting passed. Eight actual crate archives, 57 dependency checksums, nine README fences on stable/MSRV, four stable native consumers and both README entry points passed.\n- Discovery regressions: same eight cases fail six before correction and pass all eight afterward. Twenty actual early-startup cancellations, ten per browser, verify direct-child reaping and profile ownership.\n- Separate source-scoped allocation studies preserve Rust-driver event accounting and independent Firefox browser-memory observations, including remaining retention and invalid first captures. Finite runs do not establish universal leak freedom.\n\n[Run 37987315249](https://github.com/rsasaki0109/rustwright/actions/runs/37987315249) at source `be1b065` completed with six successful jobs and a failed alternate-Chrome sandbox preflight; the new headed/version/site phases were unrun. The selected helper was correctly installed, but DOM capture hit its outer deadline. Correction `3d447e72` adds the exact Chrome151-supported 10-second internal capture bound while preserving strict normal-exit, no-outer-timeout and fixture-title/body requirements. Four synthetic-process controls pass, including rejection of timeout with exit0 and full DOM; native correction verification remains pending.\n\nThe correction and frozen records are pushed at `66d98a9fcfa9ee744aae768cb06e472b2cef79d5`. [New dispatch 37990278021](https://github.com/rsasaki0109/rustwright/actions/runs/37990278021) tests that direct branch head with all seven jobs. All 153 relevant input blobs/modes match the correction source. Headed, alternate-version and public-site completion is not yet claimed. Local failed/interrupted matrices and aggregate public-site operation failures remain separately preserved.\n\n[CI evidence](https://github.com/rsasaki0109/rustwright/blob/codex/reliability-95-ci/docs/CI_VERIFICATION.md) and the [checkpoint draft](https://github.com/rsasaki0109/rustwright/blob/codex/reliability-95-ci/docs/RELIABILITY_95_CHECKPOINT.md) retain exact source identities, raw results, official artifact digests and SHA256 manifests. Evidence documents are being finalized on this branch.\n\nUnknown remote IDs after lost acknowledgments, persistent cleanup refusal, descendant-process guarantees, unexplained browser-memory retention and broader comparative workloads remain limits. Registry publication and a general SOTA claim remain separate. This stays a draft PR.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-09T14:31:32Z","updated_at":"2026-10-09T21:37:25Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"a2191f83923497f1e34a7785f316e142206dda54","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"rsasaki0109:codex/reliability-95-ci","ref":"codex/reliability-95-ci","repo":{"id":1377232899,"node_id":"R_kgDOUhboAw","name":"rustwright","full_name":"rsasaki0109/rustwright","owner":{"login":"rsasaki0109","id":18298605,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4Mjk4NjA1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18298605?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsasaki0109","html_url":"https://github.com/rsasaki0109","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsasaki0109/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsasaki0109/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsasaki0109/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsasaki0109/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsasaki0109/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsasaki0109/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsasaki0109/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsasaki0109/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsasaki0109/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":false,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"de